※ `mut` before a name marks a field of a record.  A sum holds one of its
※ variants, and is changed by being given another: there is no part of it that
※ stays while another changes.

type Either = mut one : u8 | two : u16

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    0u6
